---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import ownerPhoto from '../assets/owner-hannah.png';
import { business, manufacturer } from '../data/site';
---

<!--
  Replaces the old "you're a brand-new company" callout. With no reviews yet, a face, a name
  and the family tie are the strongest available trust signal: a prospect can see who is
  coming to their house, and the thirty-year factory stops reading as a vendor arrangement
  that could end.

  Deliberately does not say the company is new. The page answers that objection exactly once,
  in the FAQ, where a prospect who is actually asking it will look — raising it here (and in
  the Gallery, where it also used to appear) just kept telling buyers the thing we least want
  front of mind. Positive proof instead: specialist, one accountable person, family factory.

  Deliberately absent: the retailer-not-a-contractor / no-GC-licence point the old callout
  also carried. Per the owner, licensing is not raised here. Do not add it back.

  The Devlin family relationship traces to `manufacturer.relationship` in data/site.ts.
  First name only: the owner's surname is unconfirmed. OPEN — add it once known.
-->
<section id="about" class="bg-ivory-100 py-20 md:py-28">
  <div class="container-page grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,22rem)_1fr] lg:gap-16">
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[15rem] sm:max-w-xs lg:mx-0 lg:max-w-none" data-reveal>
      <Image
        src={ownerPhoto}
        alt={`Hannah, owner of ${business.name}`}
        widths={[352, 528, 704]}
        sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 22rem, (min-width: 640px) 20rem, 15rem"
        loading="lazy"
        class="w-full rounded-2xl object-cover shadow-lg ring-1 ring-olive-900/10"
      />
    </div>

    <div data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow text-olive-500">About Us</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-4xl leading-tight tracking-tight text-olive-900 sm:text-5xl">
        Hi, I&rsquo;m Hannah. Shutters are the family business.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-olive-700">
        Gulf Shore Shutters is a small business in Cape Coral, and I run it. When you call, you get
        me. When someone comes to your house with full-size samples and a tape measure, that is me
        too — not a commissioned salesperson working a script, and not a different rep every time you
        have a question.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-olive-700">
        Your shutters are built by {manufacturer.name} in {manufacturer.city}, and Devlin is family:
        my uncle is one of the owners. They have been manufacturing shutters here for over
        {manufacturer.yearsInBusiness} years, and their team does the final measure and the
        installation. So this is not a supplier I found and could walk away from — it is my family&rsquo;s
        factory, twenty minutes up the road, and my name goes on every job that leaves it.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-olive-700">
        Shutters are the only thing we sell, so that is the only thing I have to be good at. You get
        one person who answers for the whole job &mdash; from the first phone call to the last panel
        hung &mdash; and a thirty-year factory&rsquo;s product behind it.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <a
          href="#quote"
          data-cta="about-quote"
          class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-olive-600 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-ivory-50 transition hover:bg-olive-700"
        >
          Book a free consultation
        </a>
        <a
          href={`tel:${business.phoneHref}`}
          data-cta="about-call"
          class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-olive-200 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-olive-800 transition hover:bg-olive-50"
        >
          Call or text {business.phone}
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
